'' RUN: sgn over any integer is INTEGER and over a float keeps the float's type, as fbc
'' types it: it was LONG for all, so 'hex( sgn( clng( -4 ) ), 11 )' printed 000FFFFFFFF and
'' 'sgn( d ) / 4' integer-divided. Found by build/difflane.sh, seed 235.
'' Output identical to fbc-modern's.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/sgn-type.bas -o tests/codegen/sgntype.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/sgntype.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: -1              1            FFFFFFFFFFF   -1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: -0.25          0.25
